## still manual

- **imagine**: New Imagine images (views, wall plates, detail crops) are never generated by this tool: it writes the request batch, a human/agent runs imagine.py with approval.
- **mount**: First mount of a NEW object type into the game page (one import + one call in the biome main module) is a code change reviewed by hand; afterwards the staging page reloads the assets by itself.
- **swap**: Staging -> live swap + ?v bump stays a human decision after the report (gate PASS is required, not sufficient).
- **phone**: Real-phone fps (S20 FE) is measured by SmiR; the box has no GPU (SwiftShader timings are relative only).
- **checklist**: Key checklist items need a Grok-vision or owner pass record (object-gate records/); NEEDS_REVIEW otherwise.

